                    RSDKModding attribution

The launcher builds Sonic Mania from the upstream project:

    https://github.com/RSDKModding/Sonic-Mania-Decompilation

Sonic-Mania-Decompilation and the RSDKv5 engine are created and maintained by
RSDKModding and its contributors. ChaosLauncher fetches that source at build
time into a local application cache; it does not claim authorship of it and
does not relicense it.

The fetched engine/source code remains governed by its own upstream terms,
including the RSDKv5 Decompilation License, which is strictly non-commercial.
Users must consult the license files in the fetched checkout before using or
redistributing any resulting build. ChaosLauncher does not bundle game assets,
Data.rsdk files, or prebuilt game binaries in its own source, release packages,
or AppImage. Users must supply their own legally obtained Data.rsdk. A
default-off Settings option can copy the user's selected file into a generated
output folder on the user's machine for personal local use only; such outputs
must not be shared, distributed, or uploaded publicly. The Android port reads
the user's own Data.rsdk and mods from the device's shared RSDK/v5 directory;
no game assets are bundled into the APK.

                    Vendored Android build sources

The pinned upstream Android project expects local libogg and libtheora sources
that are absent from the checkout. ChaosLauncher vendors verified upstream
source archives solely as offline build inputs:

  * libogg 1.3.5       - https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/ogg/
  * libtheora 1.1.1    - https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/theora/

These libraries are from Xiph.Org and remain under their respective upstream
license terms, included inside the archives. They are not game assets and are
not distributed as part of a produced APK beyond compiled native code required
by the engine.

